{"name":"Clover Pink","hex":"#cd9bc4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clover","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the genus Trifolium with leaves usually divided into three (rarely four) leaflets and with white or red flowers.","The second Lenormand card, representing hope, optimism and short-term luck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clover"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clover","blocks":[{"text":"Clovers, also called trefoils, are plants of the genus Trifolium. They are herbaceous plants growing up to 30 cm (12 in) tall. The leaves are usually trifoliate and the small flowers are reddish to white or yellow. Related genera with similar common names include Melilotus and Medicago (burclover)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/79_Trifolium_repens_L.jpg/330px-79_Trifolium_repens_L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clover","wikidata":"Q101538"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum